WEBVTT

1
00:00:32.416 --> 00:00:38.375
<b>Here, Krishna compares a person </b>
<b>of steady wisdom to a vast ocean.</b>

2
00:00:38.375 --> 00:00:39.666
<b>He says that</b>

3
00:00:39.666 --> 00:00:44.708
<b>countless rivers pour their </b>
<b>endless waters into the ocean,</b>

4
00:00:44.708 --> 00:00:50.500
<b>yet all these rivers combined cannot disturb it,</b>

5
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:55.083
<b>their waters cannot break its peace,</b>

6
00:00:55.083 --> 00:00:58.208
<b>but rather merge into it.</b>

7
00:00:58.208 --> 00:00:59.500
<b>Similarly,</b>

8
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:06.291
<b>the countless desires of this world </b>
<b>cannot disturb a person of steady wisdom;</b>

9
00:01:06.291 --> 00:01:10.958
<b>they dissolve within them </b>
<b>without disrupting their peace.</b>

10
00:01:10.958 --> 00:01:12.375
<b>In contrast,</b>

11
00:01:12.375 --> 00:01:19.375
<b> those consumed by desires </b>
<b>never experience such peace.</b>

12
00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:25.875
<b>Our senses</b>

13
00:01:25.875 --> 00:01:29.833
<b>are constantly surrounded </b>
<b>by pleasurable temptations,</b>

14
00:01:29.833 --> 00:01:36.583
<b>and in a world of such countless allurements, </b>
<b>desires easily awaken.</b>

15
00:01:36.583 --> 00:01:37.416
<b>But</b>

16
00:01:37.416 --> 00:01:42.125
<b>one who maintains control </b>
<b>over their mind and senses,</b>

17
00:01:42.125 --> 00:01:44.166
<b>whose intellect remains steady,</b>

18
00:01:44.166 --> 00:01:48.666
<b>possesses such blissful spiritual essence</b>

19
00:01:48.666 --> 00:01:52.875
<b>that all worldly desires </b>
<b>become powerless before it.</b>

20
00:01:52.875 --> 00:02:02.583
<b>Desires dissolve in such a person just </b>
<b>as river waters merge into the ocean.</b>

21
00:02:02.583 --> 00:02:03.458
<b>Rivers</b>

22
00:02:03.458 --> 00:02:06.875
<b>and their waters cannot disturb the ocean.</b>

23
00:02:06.875 --> 00:02:07.916
<b>Similarly,</b>

24
00:02:07.916 --> 00:02:10.375
<b>the many objects of the senses</b>

25
00:02:10.375 --> 00:02:16.791
<b>and their experiences are unable to </b>
<b>disturb a person of steady wisdom.</b>

26
00:02:16.791 --> 00:02:17.666
<b>But</b>

27
00:02:17.666 --> 00:02:20.083
<b>how is this possible?</b>

28
00:02:20.083 --> 00:02:27.583
<b>The heart of a person with steady </b>
<b>wisdom is deep and vast like an ocean.</b>

29
00:02:27.583 --> 00:02:31.375
<b>And just as an ocean is already filled with water,</b>

30
00:02:31.375 --> 00:02:36.958
<b>their heart is so filled with spiritual joy</b>

31
00:02:36.958 --> 00:02:42.125
<b>that any worldly desire dissolves within it,</b>

32
00:02:42.125 --> 00:02:47.333
<b>just as a small river loses itself in the ocean.</b>

33
00:02:47.333 --> 00:02:49.875
<b>Consider it this way –</b>

34
00:02:49.875 --> 00:02:53.291
<b>it's like someone who has </b>
<b>eaten to complete satisfaction.</b>

35
00:02:53.291 --> 00:03:00.791
<b>Their stomach has no room for more food, </b>
<b>thus no craving for it.</b>

36
00:03:00.791 --> 00:03:04.958
<b>A person of steady wisdom's </b>
<b>mind is so filled with joy</b>

37
00:03:04.958 --> 00:03:09.375
<b>that no space remains for worldly cravings.</b>

38
00:03:09.375 --> 00:03:11.166
<b>In direct contrast,</b>

39
00:03:11.166 --> 00:03:14.916
<b>one whose mind lacks spiritual joy</b>

40
00:03:14.916 --> 00:03:18.166
<b>searches for happiness in materialism,</b>

41
00:03:18.166 --> 00:03:20.166
<b>seeks it in objects.</b>

42
00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:23.583
<b>But this search is like a mirage</b>

43
00:03:23.583 --> 00:03:27.583
<b>where a thirsty person sees water everywhere,</b>

44
00:03:27.583 --> 00:03:34.625
<b>yet upon reaching finds </b>
<b>not water but only its illusion.</b>

45
00:03:34.625 --> 00:03:38.708
<b>Material pleasure is such an illusion.</b>

46
00:03:38.708 --> 00:03:40.791
<b>Where happiness appears</b>

47
00:03:40.791 --> 00:03:41.833
<b>but</b>

48
00:03:41.833 --> 00:03:43.416
<b>doesn't exist.</b>

49
00:03:43.416 --> 00:03:46.750
<b>The person remains forever thirsty.</b>

50
00:03:50.958 --> 00:03:57.000
<b>In this world full of temptations, </b>
<b>the arising of desires is very natural.</b>

51
00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:58.416
<b>However,</b>

52
00:03:58.416 --> 00:04:02.208
<b>whether to control these </b>
<b>desires and master them,</b>

53
00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:02.916
<b>or</b>

54
00:04:02.916 --> 00:04:11.625
<b>become enslaved by them, </b>
<b>this choice lies with each person.</b>

55
00:04:11.625 --> 00:04:16.958
<b>One who becomes enslaved wanders endlessly,</b>

56
00:04:16.958 --> 00:04:19.166
<b>pursuing each desire,</b>

57
00:04:19.166 --> 00:04:24.458
<b>expecting to find peace in their fulfillment,</b>

58
00:04:24.458 --> 00:04:27.166
<b>but finds none.</b>

59
00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:32.291
<b>What they find instead is </b>
<b>only agitation and restlessness.</b>

60
00:04:32.291 --> 00:04:33.458
<b>So then,</b>

61
00:04:33.458 --> 00:04:38.791
<b>who is capable of controlling these desires?</b>

62
00:04:38.791 --> 00:04:41.916
<b>One who is content in life</b>

63
00:04:41.916 --> 00:04:45.708
<b>One who is grateful for every moment</b>

64
00:04:45.708 --> 00:04:50.041
<b>One who isn't wandering in constant </b>
<b>search of pleasure and happiness,</b>

65
00:04:50.041 --> 00:04:50.791
<b>but</b>

66
00:04:50.791 --> 00:04:57.750
<b>has realized the truth that joy and </b>
<b>happiness lie not outside, but within.</b>

67
00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:03.708
<b>And by diving into their spiritual depths, </b>
<b>they have found this happiness.</b>

68
00:05:03.708 --> 00:05:06.250
<b>This happiness resides within everyone,</b>

69
00:05:06.250 --> 00:05:08.250
<b>within you too.</b>

70
00:05:08.250 --> 00:05:11.083
<b>Recognize your life's purpose,</b>

71
00:05:11.083 --> 00:05:13.291
<b>dive into the depths of your soul,</b>

72
00:05:13.291 --> 00:05:16.958
<b>and once you do this,</b>

73
00:05:16.958 --> 00:05:21.750
<b>worldly cravings will seem trivial.</b>

74
00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:26.458
<b>Controlling them will no longer be difficult.</b>

75
00:05:26.458 --> 00:05:29.000
<b>I am your charioteer too,</b>

76
00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:32.291
<b>and I will guide you into these depths of the soul,</b>

77
00:05:32.291 --> 00:05:35.708
<b>to witness life's truth.</b>

78
00:05:35.708 --> 00:05:37.791
<b>Are you ready?</b>

79
00:05:37.791 --> 00:05:38.833
<b>Come,</b>

80
00:05:38.833 --> 00:05:40.833
<b>let us proceed together.</b>

81
00:05:45.125 --> 00:05:50.666
<b>The ocean contains all river waters within itself,</b>

82
00:05:50.666 --> 00:05:54.208
<b>never letting them spill over.</b>

83
00:05:54.208 --> 00:05:55.625
<b>Similarly, </b>

84
00:05:55.625 --> 00:05:59.708
<b>a trustworthy person's hallmark is that</b>

85
00:05:59.708 --> 00:06:07.666
<b>they contain within themselves others' sensitive </b>
<b>matters and problems shared with them,</b>

86
00:06:07.666 --> 00:06:11.166
<b>never letting them overflow.</b>

87
00:06:11.166 --> 00:06:17.208
<b>While others don't delay</b>
<b>in spreading shared secrets.</b>

88
00:06:17.208 --> 00:06:21.791
<b>They eagerly tell others.</b>

89
00:06:21.791 --> 00:06:24.583
<b>Why does one do this?</b>

90
00:06:24.583 --> 00:06:25.875
<b>Naturally,</b>

91
00:06:25.875 --> 00:06:31.208
<b>the shallower one is, the more they overflow.</b>

92
00:06:31.208 --> 00:06:35.458
<b>Choose depth. Develop it.</b>

93
00:06:35.458 --> 00:06:39.291
<b>When you choose spiritual depth,</b>

94
00:06:39.291 --> 00:06:45.583
<b>you'll see others through eyes </b>
<b>of empathy and understanding.</b>

95
00:06:45.583 --> 00:06:51.000
<b>Such a person becomes worthy </b>
<b>of everyone's affection and trust.</b>

96
00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:53.333
<b>How beautiful would be a society</b>

97
00:06:53.333 --> 00:06:56.500
<b>where humans love humans,</b>

98
00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:59.958
<b>trust one another.</b>

99
00:06:59.958 --> 00:07:02.458
<b>Society is you</b>

100
00:07:02.458 --> 00:07:06.583
<b>- begin this change from yourself.</b>

101
00:07:11.416 --> 00:07:16.541
<b>Mutual cooperation is the key </b>
<b>to success in professional life.</b>

102
00:07:16.541 --> 00:07:18.666
<b>For this, it's important that</b>

103
00:07:18.666 --> 00:07:22.625
<b>you can work harmoniously with everyone.</b>

104
00:07:22.625 --> 00:07:28.875
<b>This happens only when you </b>
<b>can respect diverse thoughts</b>

105
00:07:28.875 --> 00:07:34.708
<b>while protecting yourself from</b>
<b>being overwhelmed by them.</b>

106
00:07:34.708 --> 00:07:41.958
<b>Clean or muddy, the ocean accepts </b>
<b>various waters from rivers,</b>

107
00:07:41.958 --> 00:07:43.166
<b>yet</b>

108
00:07:43.166 --> 00:07:46.500
<b>doesn't change its essential nature.</b>

109
00:07:46.500 --> 00:07:54.791
<b>Only one whose heart is vast like the ocean, </b>
<b>and deep too, can achieve this.</b>

110
00:07:54.791 --> 00:07:58.208
<b>When you understand your spiritual nature,</b>

111
00:07:58.208 --> 00:08:02.458
<b>you'll develop an inner security that protects you</b>

112
00:08:02.458 --> 00:08:07.416
<b>from being unduly influenced by others' thoughts.</b>

113
00:08:07.416 --> 00:08:13.041
<b>Then you can understand people's </b>
<b>mindsets without aversion.</b>

114
00:08:13.041 --> 00:08:15.583
<b>Such a person remains peaceful,</b>

115
00:08:15.583 --> 00:08:18.916
<b>understands all, respects them,</b>

116
00:08:18.916 --> 00:08:20.041
<b>while</b>

117
00:08:20.041 --> 00:08:24.916
<b>remaining steady in their own life values.</b>

